<Container version="2">
  <Name>Frameleaf</Name>
  <Repository>ghcr.io/frameleaf/frameleaf-manager:latest</Repository>
  <Registry>https://github.com/orgs/Frameleaf/packages/container/package/frameleaf-manager</Registry>
  <Shell>sh</Shell>
  <DefaultTagDescription>Latest published Frameleaf Manager</DefaultTagDescription>
  <Network>bridge</Network>
  <Privileged>false</Privileged>
  <Project>https://frameleaf.app</Project>
  <Support>https://frameleaf.app/help/</Support>
  <Overview>Frameleaf is your own photo and video library, running on your Unraid server. Bring a lifetime of photos home, find any moment by describing it, edit it, and enjoy it on your phone, in any browser and on the TV. Your originals stay as ordinary files on your disks, faces and search run on your own hardware, and there's no subscription or telemetry.

• Library — a fast timeline for every photo and video, with albums, folders, RAW, Live Photos and your best shots picked out.
• Search — describe what you remember: people and pets, places and landmarks, text in photos, even words spoken in videos.
• Memories — on this day, trips and years in review, played as shows on Apple TV and Android TV.
• Create — a photo editor; Studio, a real video editor that can make a movie from an album in one step; Boards for references and design files; and Clients for photography studios.
• Share — a library for each person, partner sharing, shared albums and protected links.
• Apps — iPhone, iPad and Android with camera-roll backup, plus Apple TV and Android TV.
• Keep it safe — duplicate review, locked content and backups. Optional Frameleaf Cloud adds remote access and off-site backup.

Switching? Bring your library across from Immich, PhotoPrism, LibrePhotos, Photoview, Piwigo, Lychee, PiGallery2, Ente Photos, Nextcloud Photos and Memories, or Synology Photos, and import Google Photos Takeout or iCloud Photos.

This is the official way to install Frameleaf on Unraid. Frameleaf Manager sets up Frameleaf, its database and optional machine learning, then handles updates and database backups from one dashboard. Click Apply to install with the suggested folders, or change any folder first. Then open Manager and create your administrator from your home network. Frameleaf is in beta: keep your own backup of original photos and videos.</Overview>
  <Category>MediaApp:Photos MediaApp:Video</Category>
  <ExtraSearchTerms>photos videos photo-library photo-backup google-photos icloud gallery albums family faces people search memories video-editor ai self-hosted immich photoprism librephotos photoview piwigo lychee pigallery2 ente nextcloud-photos synology-photos</ExtraSearchTerms>
  <Requires>Docker enabled. The folders below are ready to use; to store anything elsewhere, change only its folder path. Frameleaf Manager uses the Docker socket to install and update Frameleaf. See the setup guide for hardware requirements.</Requires>
  <Icon>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/frameleaf-app/main/design/frameleaf/mark.png</Icon>
  <Discord>https://discord.gg/cN3U3mv4</Discord>
  <Reddit>https://www.reddit.com/r/Frameleaf/</Reddit>
  <Twitter>https://x.com/frameleafapp</Twitter>
  <DonateLink>https://frameleaf.app/pricing/#supporter</DonateLink>
  <DonateText>Support Frameleaf with a supporter licence</DonateText>
  <Photo>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-library.jpg</Photo>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-library.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-search.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-people.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-memories.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-editor.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-studio.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-boards.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/frameleaf-apple-tv.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Screenshot>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/images/manager-overview.jpg</Screenshot>
  <Video>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=rNgyZZoZoEg</Video>
  <Video>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=INeVz9NFzOM</Video>
  <Video>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=bTfFBDHc6OE</Video>
  <TemplateURL>https://raw.githubusercontent.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/main/templates/frameleaf-manager.xml</TemplateURL>
  <ReadMe>https://frameleaf.app/docs/nas/unraid/</ReadMe>
  <License>https://github.com/Frameleaf/unraid-apps/blob/main/LICENSE</License>
  <WebUI>https://[IP]:[PORT:9443]</WebUI>
  <ExtraParams>--label app.frameleaf.manager.role=controller --security-opt no-new-privileges --cap-drop ALL --cap-add CHOWN --cap-add DAC_OVERRIDE --cap-add FOWNER</ExtraParams>
  <Config Name="Manager port" Target="9443" Default="2282" Mode="tcp" Description="Port you open Manager on. 2282 sits next to Frameleaf (2283) and avoids 9443, which Portainer and other apps often use" Type="Port" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false">2282</Config>
  <Config Name="Manager origin" Target="MANAGER_ORIGIN" Default="" Description="Optional. Leave blank to open Manager by IP address or tower.local. For a custom name or HTTP access, enter the exact HTTP or HTTPS address with port (for example http://tower.local:2282) and set Advanced View WebUI to match. HTTP is unencrypted; use a trusted network." Type="Variable" Display="always" Required="false" Mask="false"></Config>
  <Config Name="Manager state" Target="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-manager" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-manager" Mode="rw" Description="Manager's own settings. Use the suggested folder or choose any folder on your server." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-manager</Config>
  <Config Name="Media" Target="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-media" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-media" Mode="rw" Description="Your original photos and videos. Use the suggested folder or choose any folder on your server." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-media</Config>
  <Config Name="Database parent" Target="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases" Mode="rw" Description="The Frameleaf database. Use the suggested folder or choose any folder on a local disk, outside Docker data/docker.img." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases</Config>
  <Config Name="Database backups" Target="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-backups" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-backups" Mode="rw" Description="Encrypted database-only checkpoints. Use the suggested folder or choose any folder on your server. Does not back up media." Type="Path" Display="always" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-backups</Config>
  <Config Name="State path" Target="MANAGER_DATA" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-manager" Description="Leave this as it is. Manager finds your folder from the mapping above." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-manager</Config>
  <Config Name="Media roots" Target="MANAGER_STORAGE_ROOTS" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-media" Description="Leave this as it is unless you add more media folders. Separate container paths with colons; each must be mapped above." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-media</Config>
  <Config Name="Database roots" Target="MANAGER_DATABASE_ROOTS" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases" Description="Leave this as it is unless you add more database folders. Separate container paths with colons; each must be mapped above." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases</Config>
  <Config Name="Database default" Target="MANAGER_APPDATA_ROOT" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases" Description="Leave this as it is. The database folder setup suggests first." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-databases</Config>
  <Config Name="Backup path" Target="MANAGER_BACKUP_ROOT" Default="/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-backups" Description="Leave this as it is. Manager finds your folder from the mapping above." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/mnt/user/appdata/frameleaf-backups</Config>
  <Config Name="Frameleaf address" Target="MANAGER_BIND_ADDRESS" Default="0.0.0.0" Description="Where the Frameleaf app it installs is published. 0.0.0.0 makes it reachable from other devices on your network; 127.0.0.1 limits it to this server." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">0.0.0.0</Config>
  <Config Name="Platform" Target="MANAGER_PLATFORM" Default="unraid" Description="Unraid host integration; keep this value." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">unraid</Config>
  <Config Name="Docker socket" Target="/var/run/docker.sock" Default="/var/run/docker.sock" Mode="rw" Description="Allows Manager to create and control sibling containers on this host." Type="Path" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/var/run/docker.sock</Config>
  <Config Name="DockerMan templates" Target="/run/frameleaf-host/templates-user" Default="/boot/config/plugins/dockerMan/templates-user" Mode="rw" Description="Saves per-container templates so Frameleaf services can also be edited and recreated by Unraid DockerMan." Type="Path" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/boot/config/plugins/dockerMan/templates-user</Config>
  <Config Name="Host mount information" Target="/run/frameleaf-host/mountinfo" Default="/proc/1/mountinfo" Mode="ro" Description="Read-only host filesystem evidence for database storage checks." Type="Path" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/proc/1/mountinfo</Config>
  <Config Name="Unraid Docker configuration" Target="/run/frameleaf-host/docker.cfg" Default="/boot/config/docker.cfg" Mode="ro" Description="Read-only Unraid appdata and Docker storage configuration." Type="Path" Display="advanced" Required="true" Mask="false">/boot/config/docker.cfg</Config>
  <Config Name="Unraid autostart file" Target="/run/frameleaf-host/unraid-autostart" Default="" Mode="rw" Description="Optional override. Leave blank: Manager automatically discovers and accesses Docker's existing Unraid autostart list for imports and recovery." Type="Path" Display="advanced" Required="false" Mask="false"></Config>
  <Config Name="Autostart controller path" Target="MANAGER_UNRAID_AUTOSTART" Default="" Description="Optional override for an existing manual autostart mapping. Leave blank for automatic configuration." Type="Variable" Display="advanced" Required="false" Mask="false"></Config>
</Container>
